sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant G as Gateway<br/>(MCP tool call)
    participant M as mqtt_task<br/>Core 0
    participant S as MCPServer<br/>onDownlink()
    participant W as mcp_worker<br/>Core 1
    participant N as net_task<br/>Core 0
    G->>M: REQ tool=0x02 read_telemetry rid=R flags=ACK_REQUESTED<br/>args {1: sections}
    M->>S: onDownlink(data, len) — data owned by esp-mqtt
    Note over S: checkDownlink: magic, version, type, length,<br/>size ≤ 4096, tool registered, rid not seen
    S->>S: free_q.receive(slot, 0 ticks)  (none → ERR BUSY retryAfterMs 250)
    S->>S: memcpy frame → slot · deadline = now + deadlineMs (5 s default)
    S->>N: ACK {queueDepth, etaMs} via tx_q (before the job is visible)
    S->>W: job_q.send(slot, 0 ticks)  (PRIORITY → sendToFront)
    S-->>M: return within microseconds, MQTT keeps running
    N->>G: ACK
    W->>W: cancelled? expired? → ERR CANCELLED / DEADLINE_EXCEEDED
    W->>W: uplink.acquire(≤ 200 ms) · handler writes CBOR after a 22-byte gap
    Note over W: parseArgs: map, no duplicate keys,<br/>sections ≤ 0xFF else ERR INVALID_ARGS argKey 1
    W->>W: collect heap · net · cpu · tasks · sensors · actuators
    W->>W: memmove → {1: timing, 2: result} · validate · free slot
    W->>N: uplink.submit(RES) via tx_q
    N->>G: RES status OK (one esp_mqtt_client_enqueue)
